A||||43||GT Bastard||Here's an entertaining video of me tearing up some pavement in my car...||||7||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||01-18-2001||09:00 PM|||| <A HREF="http://pimpn8ntez.tripod.com/sloiero.mpg" TARGET=_blank>http://pimpn8ntez.tripod.com/sloiero.mpg</A> <P>This footage was taken a couple weeks ago in about 40 degree weather(hence the excessive wheelspin.)  The quality is really good, but it's a very large download(22 megs I think.)  One of the reasons for making this video is because the next time I drive the car out of it's garage, it will be on it's way down to a friends shop to begin the teardown process.  At this time it will recieve a fresh 3.2 and a new ACT clutch.  If you listen closely, you'll hear some bearing noise before I go into reverse(dissapears above 3500rpm or so...)  Both launches are 2000rpm clutch dumps(4-puck race clutch.)  On hot pavement it hooks up, but you'll see what happens in the video.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>ps- The guy with the evil laugh is Fierogod(Brad)<P>Yes, I know know the hood is black and the car is dirty.  Paint should be coming around Summer.  Hey, at least I buffed it and washed it before putting it away!<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||7
